# DISABLED 2026-09-18 (.disable suffix — the app-of-apps directory ignores it).
#
# WHY: ollama's compiled-in `PARSER qwen3-coder` never engages when the model omits the
# opening <tool_call> tag, so the whole tool call leaks into message content as literal
#     <function=NAME><parameter=K>…</parameter></function></tool_call>
# (note the orphan closing tag) and the agent executes NOTHING — every turn ends
# finish_reason=stop, tool_turns=0, with the call printed as prose. That is
# ollama/ollama#16686, OPEN since 2026-06-12, with fixes #17742/#16398/#17021 all
# unmerged; no ollama release fixes it. Measured with the eda-pcb-agent's real 38 tool
# schemas: ollama 4/4 FAILED, vLLM 0/4 failed.
#
# Thor now serves `thor/qwen3.6-35b-a3b-nvfp4` from vLLM instead (app-of-apps/vllm.yaml),
# which parses the same XML shape correctly via --tool-call-parser qwen3_xml. The two are
# EXCLUSIVE on the single non-shareable GPU anyway, so only one can run.
#
# ⚠ SEPARATE FROM ollama-turing, which is a DIFFERENT app in a different namespace on the
# discrete-GPU node and is NOT affected by this. `turing/*` routes keep working.
#
# ⚠ ITS IMAGE CANNOT CURRENTLY BE REBUILT even if re-enabled: the build dies fetching
# github.com/klauspost/compress@v1.18.3 (proxy.golang.org 302 -> a target that resets the
# TLS connection, reproduced from outside the cluster). See ollama/build-files-configmap.yaml.
#
# TO RE-ENABLE: `git mv ollama.yaml.disable ollama.yaml`, push, then
# `scripts/runtime/switchLLMBackend.sh ollama` — which scales vLLM to 0 first, because the
# GPU cannot hold both. Re-check #16686 before trusting it with a tool-calling agent, and
# repoint the consumers that were moved to the vLLM route (hermes, open-webui).
#
# ArgoCD Application: Ollama (GGUF/llama.cpp server on the Jetson-Thor GPU).
# IN-CLUSTER ONLY — no Ingress; the sole client is the LiteLLM gateway
# (route `coder-ollama`).
#
# EXCLUSIVE with vLLM: one Thor GPU, one backend at a time. The Deployment ships
# replicas: 0 (vLLM owns the GPU by default); scripts/runtime/switchLLMBackend.sh
# flips which backend runs. ignoreDifferences below keeps ArgoCD's selfHeal from
# reverting the runtime scale (the twin ignore lives in vllm.yaml).
#
# Manifests: deployment.yaml + build-files-configmap.yaml + postsync-build-image.yaml
# (the CI build seed/trigger, a PreSync hook despite the name) + presync-registry-cred.yaml
# (mints the image pull secret BEFORE the Deployment — PreSync, else ImagePullBackOff
# deadlocks). The image is built by GitLab CI (ollama v0.32.1 for Thor), not ArgoCD.
#
# placement.ecc/tier: mesh — the pod runs on the mesh GPU node (not cloud).
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: ollama
  namespace: argocd-apps
  annotations:
    placement.ecc/tier: mesh
spec:
  project: default
  source:
    repoURL: git@github.com:YourProject/yourGit.git
    targetRevision: main
    path: deployment/argocd-apps/ollama
    directory:
      # Only k8s manifests sync. The Dockerfile/.gitlab-ci.yml are CI build inputs
      # (mirrored into GitLab by the build-trigger via build-files-configmap.yaml),
      # not cluster objects; *.sh + README are dev docs.
      exclude: "{*.sh,README.md,Dockerfile,.gitlab-ci.yml}"
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: ollama
  # The switch script scales this Deployment 0↔1 at runtime. Without this ignore,
  # automated selfHeal would snap replicas back to the git value (0) minutes after
  # every switch-up, killing the running backend.
  ignoreDifferences:
    - group: apps
      kind: Deployment
      name: ollama
      namespace: ollama
      jsonPointers:
        - /spec/replicas
  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      prune: true
      selfHeal: true
    syncOptions:
      - CreateNamespace=true
      - ServerSideApply=true
      # ignoreDifferences only affects diffing by default; this makes the SYNC
      # itself respect the ignored field (don't overwrite live replicas on sync).
      - RespectIgnoreDifferences=true
    # Retry forever: on recreate the PreSync hooks (build-trigger + registry-cred)
    # race GitLab bring-up. Without retry a single hook failure leaves the app Failed
    # until a git change. Same as vLLM.
    retry:
      limit: -1
      backoff:
        duration: 30s
        factor: 2
        maxDuration: 5m
